      "problem": "Simplify $\\dfrac{x^2}{x^3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We subtract the exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{3}} & = \\\\ {x}^{(2-3)} & = \\\\ {x}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we convert the negative exponent to a positive exponent by taking the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{x^3} = \\dfrac 1 x.\n$$",
